{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And these are the kings.</b> He informs us that they were compelled to appoint foreign men as kings because there was none among them fit to rule, and that they would not establish a king who was son of a king." "<b>Before any king reigned.</b> Before Moses would reign over them by command of the blessed El, as it says: וַיְצַוֵּם אֶל בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (Exodus 6:23), after the manner of וְצִוְּךָ לְנָגִיד (1 Samuel 25:30). But once a king did reign, the kingdom of Esau ceased and they became clan-chiefs (אַלּוּפִים), in accordance with וּלְאֹם מִלְאֹם יֶאֱמָץ (Genesis 25:23)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:29.451317906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}